  {"id":"l1-anchor","type":"story","title":"The lens for the rest of this course","body":"Whenever you meet a database mechanism, ask three questions: What expensive movement does it avoid? What work does it group together? What locality does it exploit? Those questions turn implementation details into a coherent system.","label":"CORE MODEL · REPEAT 2","accent":"Databases are designed around avoiding expensive trips down the memory hierarchy.","bullets":["Avoid the trip","Make the trip carry more useful data","Reuse the result of the trip"]}
